  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read http_profile.delegated_bound_result, delegated_unbound_result and delegated_credential_chain against the commit that last wrote the record. In the verifier: the floor and full bound-response verifiers take one BoundExchange (response, request) and signature checks take one SignatureOver (base, signature), with the same checks in the same order; sf_dictionary.rs shares one quote-aware top-level split (QuoteScan) between the dictionary and the parameter splits with the same quote, escape, separator and trim rules, and its per-member refusals sit in labelled_value in the same order; check_tail_spelling's refusals moved into has_empty_segment and has_space_outside_quotes behind the same single error; the profile-tag test is `!= Some(PROFILE_TAG)` where it was a match with the same refusal. In the delegation module the three revocation identifiers are tested together with the same DelegationRevoked refusal and the cnf self-consistency test moved into cnf_is_self_consistent unchanged. delegation_e2e_test became a directory (fixtures, signing, verify); each cited test keeps its name, expected HttpProfileError, epoch set, revocation and verification instant (Checks::STANDARD is the credential's epoch, nothing revoked, NOW; the stale-epoch and revoked-key tests state their own). The claim, premises and dependencies are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor, and every tested symbol the unit names still names a test function.",
